WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:02.535
Colonel Leighton, what is going on?

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.004
This is the latest incident,

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:07.507
this third shootdown of of a craft.

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:08.608
First it was a balloon.

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:11.011
Now we have these unidentified objects

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:12.612
in a week.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:13.813
What are your thoughts

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:15.048
as you're looking at all of this?

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:15.715
Is this

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:16.016
you know,

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:16.950
these things are shot down

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.185
and as an abundance of caution and,

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:19.486
you know,

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:20.587
they're on our radar screen

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:21.321
and we're looking for them

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.790
because it's top of mind.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:24.224
Or is there

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:25.358
something more to be concerned

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:25.992
about here?

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:27.027
Well, I think, Jim, the

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.661
the big thing is that obviously there's

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.196
heightened awareness now at this point.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.131
So, you know,

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:31.698
you had the incident

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.600
a week ago where we shot down

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.135
the Chinese surveillance balloon

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:36.169
who were pretty convinced that

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:38.004
that's exactly what that was.

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:38.671
And then we started

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.407
seeing all these other objects.

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.809
Clearly, the radar operators for North

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:44.210
are very sensitive

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.678
now to anything

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:46.980
that even looks remotely

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.449
like an unusual object in the skies.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:51.718
And the fact of the matter is, is,

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:52.052
you know,

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:53.787
when you look at where these other two

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:56.089
objects, the second and the third object

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.358
where they were,

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:00.827
the second one was near Prudhoe Bay,

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.495
which is a major energy

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.631
production area for the United States.

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:06.800
And then you look at the third

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:07.700
one over the Yukon,

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.736
also rich in resources

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:10.770
So there are

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.405
all kinds of possibilities here.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:13.406
Could it be a weather balloon?

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:14.707
Absolutely.

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.242
Are there other things that it could be?

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:16.776
Yes.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.511
We just have to really find out

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.180
exactly what kinds of things these are.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.481
But it's very clear

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.516
that at least in one instances,

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:24.384
one instance,

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:27.320
we've had a testing of the American

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.889
and Canadian air defense systems

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.291
in the other two instances,

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.926
that could also be the case.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.360
And so we have to really assess

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.429
where these came from and what they

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:37.864
what the capabilities of these

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:38.531
objects are.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.666
Is it a little strange

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.968
that we're we're about a day

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:42.936
or more than a day

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:44.571
since the shooting down of that

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:45.572
object over

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.040
Alaska off the coast of Alaska?

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:47.407
And yesterday,

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:48.308
we still haven't

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:50.310
been told by the government what it is.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.211
Yeah, that's

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:52.512
that is a bit strange,

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:53.646
although I guess

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.181
we have to keep in mind that,

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.383
you know, it's a very remote location.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.685
I've been up there in that area

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:00.420
once in my Air Force career,

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.254
and it is believed

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:02.088
it's the end of the world.

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:03.590
It is literally the end of the world.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:04.924
And, you know, it's it's

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:05.825
one of those areas

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.093
where it's very hard

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:09.362
to get all the rescue missions in there

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.197
and the retrieval missions.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:13.133
So to do the forensic analysis

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.268
that is being conducted now

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:17.704
on the Chinese surveillance platform

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:19.038
that is going to take some time.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:20.073
And also keep in mind, it's

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.574
a long distance from Quantico

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.008
if they choose

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:23.877
to bring it to Quantico again.

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:24.811
So that's

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:25.745
you know, that's another reason

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:27.780
why they probably don't know exactly

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.749
what it is yet.

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:31.184
And once that happens,

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:32.986
we'll probably take a week or two

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:35.021
before we get some idea of

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:35.922
of what

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:37.790
these two last objects actually are.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:38.825
And what about this

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:40.126
element of Natasha

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:41.094
Bertrand's reporting

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:43.163
that the pilots had differing accounts

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:45.431
as to what they saw and this one

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:47.834
particular piece of information

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.435
that she just reported again

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:50.336
a few moments ago,

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.038
which I think might be giving some people

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.740
the willies, which is

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.208
the pilots could not ascertain

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:55.642
as to what

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:56.743
the propulsion system

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:58.978
was of this particular object.

00:02:59.245 --> 00:02:59.712
Yes.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.114
So, Jim, these

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:01.347
you know,

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.449
your thoughts on the pilots,

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:04.250
you know, whether they fly

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.052
by very quickly, they've got,

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:06.252
you know,

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.655
a few seconds to take a good look at

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:11.491
this craft or whatever object this is.

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:11.891
Yeah.

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:13.793
And in some cases,

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:16.696
what's called a misread is the report

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:18.498
that the pilot submits to headquarters

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:19.966
into the intelligence shop.

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:21.134
And when they look at that,

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:23.136
then they can determine it's

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:25.205
basically an eyewitness account

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:26.406
of a car crash or something

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:27.407
similar to that.

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:28.441
And when you look at that,

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.109
then you start piecing together, okay,

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:31.377
this is what they saw.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:32.579
And then you combine

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:34.881
that with the actual forensic evidence

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:36.115
of the pieces

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:36.616
and parts

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:37.650
that we're able to gather

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.352
from these incidents.

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:41.287
And then we can perhaps better ascertain

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:41.754
whether or not

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.256
there really was a propulsion system

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:44.257
where there just flew

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:46.292
along with the wind stream

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.695
or if there was some other aspect to this

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:49.529
that we don't know about,

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:49.796
are there

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:51.130
technologies that are being used

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.532
that we don't understand yet?

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:54.234
All of that is possible.

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:55.868
Unlikely, but possible

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:56.703
and so those are the things

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:57.670
we have to consider.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.172
And the possibility

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:00.440
that we might have a foreign power

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:01.107
like China

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:01.841
or Russia

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:03.276
sort of poking and prodding

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:05.211
with these objects.

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:06.145
How concerning is that

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:08.147
from a national security standpoint?

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:09.549
So these are the kinds of

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:11.384
things are a Major No-No, aren't they?

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:13.519
Well, we do that all the time.

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:14.487
We do it to them.

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:15.288
They do it to us.

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:17.190
But here's the No-No part.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.525
We don't overfly their territory.

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:21.261
They have in these cases,

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:23.162
overflown our territory

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:25.231
if it is, in fact, the objects.

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:27.400
Two and three are in fact, from either

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.434
China or Russia.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:29.535
We know that in

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:30.637
the case of the first object,

00:04:30.637 --> 00:04:31.404
the balloon,

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:32.972
obviously the Chinese did that.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.040
That was the big No-No.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.042
So the way things run in the

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:37.310
reconnaissance world now

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.345
is, yes, you test the systems,

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:41.180
but you don't overfly the systems,

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.448
the air defense systems of

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:44.083
of an adversary don't get caught.

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:46.052
And you certainly don't get caught.

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:46.586
Like, for instance,

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:48.655
Gary Powers back in the early 1960s,

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:50.123
you know who definitely got caught.

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:51.391
The rules have changed since then.

00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:52.325
So we don't do that

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:54.027
kind of thing anymore.

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:56.162
Now, when it comes to

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:57.330
these kinds of assessments,

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.431
yes, the Chinese

00:04:58.431 --> 00:04:58.965
and the Russians

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:00.300
are obviously always

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.201
testing our air defenses.

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:03.269
It's very logical

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:04.671
that they did this again.

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:06.339
Let's see if the facts bear that

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:07.206
supposition out.

